// The fonts xWorks bundles, and the families text falls back to for
// characters a family lacks, all under the SIL Open Font License 1.1:
//
// - Source Serif 4, Inter and JetBrains Mono, documents' serif, sans and
//   code (project owner, 2026-10-22, review pysc65hp);
// - Inter, the interface's font too (review frhewnk0);
// - Noto, for every script the others lack.
//
// They aren't committed: `cargo run -p fetch-fonts` downloads them into
// fonts/ from pinned commits and releases and checks each against its
// hash. CI does the same. Static faces that come only in a release's zip
// archive are taken out of it.
//
// The CJK fonts are the pan-CJK ones: each holds Japanese, Korean and both
// Chinese forms, and its `locl` feature picks them by language. Noto Serif
// falls back to the serif CJK face, Noto Sans to the sans (project owner,
// 2026-10-21).
//
// The app loads a file marked `on_demand` only once text needs a character
// the others lack. The CJK faces are 83 MB of the 87, and a document
// without CJK text never needs them (project owner, 2026-10-22, review
// 094846qg). Tests load every file.
